-- title:
--   Fibre-singular points are supersingular j-points, under a genus inequality
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and with compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose $q$-expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero, and let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the pushout of the two charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z \in X$ be a point at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and suppose $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Assume further, for some algebraically closed field $\Omega_0$ of characteristic $p$, some [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16) $w$ of level $M$ over $\Omega_0$ (a weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral $q$-expansion whose reduction in $\Omega_0((q))$ is nonzero) and the element $\bar{j}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC Ω₀ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqModC Ω₀`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), the inequality $$g\bigl(\text{laurentBaseChange of } \mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))\text{ over }\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\bigr) + 1 \le 2\,g\bigl(\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\ \Omega_0\, M\, w\bigr) + \#S,$$ where $g$ denotes [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions.html#L145), the Igusa field is the $\Omega_0$-field generated by `x1FunctionFieldC Ω₀ M` together with the inverse of the reduced $q$-expansion of $w$, and $S$ is the set of places $v$ of `x1FunctionFieldC Ω₀ M` over $\Omega_0$ (proper valuation subrings containing $\Omega_0$ whose ideals are principal) with $\bar{j}$ in the valuation subring and $v$-residue value of $\bar{j}$ in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω₀`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). Then $z$ is the image under [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L238) of a point $y$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j`, and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime corresponding to $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $p$.
--
--   This is the conditional form of the statement that the special fibre over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ is regular away from the supersingular points, in the style of the arithmetic-genus count of Deligne–Rapoport rather than the local moduli-theoretic analysis of Katz–Mazur: the only additional hypothesis is the genus inequality relating the genus of $X_1(Mp)$ to the genus of the Igusa curve and the number of supersingular points. Instantiating the auxiliary field at $\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$, where the inequality is available, yields the unconditional statement [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_iotaFin_eq_and_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_not_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_iotaFin_eq_and_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_not_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul).
